From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Kulinich <entaytion@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:03:19 +0300
Subject: Show custom title text on the dialogs list, with an option for the archive

Moved out of misc/branding.patch, where it accidentally lived as a shared
inugram patch -- this logic (DIALOGS_TITLE_TEXT + Disguise-mode title swap)
is entiny-authored and unrelated to inugram's own app rename/branding, so it
was at risk of being silently dropped or duplicated on every inugram merge.

- ChatHelper.getDialogsTitle() renders the configured title (app name,
  username, first name, or "Chats") in place of the stock Telegram logo,
  except while Disguise mode is active
- new toggle: DIALOGS_TITLE_TEXT_OVERRIDE_ARCHIVE controls whether this
  custom title also replaces "Archived Chats" on the archive screen
  (previously it always did, unconditionally, which was the actual bug)
---
